# The lake's sea state. An inland lake with six-metre walls on one side of it: short waves, a
# hand's breadth of chop, and a wind that comes off the hills to the north-east.
#
# ⚠ The zone names this file, and a name that does not resolve is not an error — the zone falls back
# to its inline spectrum and draws a perfectly convincing wrong sea. `WaterZoneSystem.UnresolvedWaves`
# is the only thing that says so, which is why `Arena.SupplyFrame` logs it.
#
# ⚠ `count` is the permutation axis and is quantised to Eight / Sixteen / ThirtyTwo, so raising the
# sea state does not compile a shader — doc 35 § D7. Eight is right for water this size; the
# wavelengths below are all shorter than the lake is wide, which is what stops the surface reading as
# one slab tilting.
name: Lake
spectrum:
  windDirection: 2.2
  windSpeed: 4.5
  directionalSpread: 0.8
  minimumWavelength: 1.5
  maximumWavelength: 9
  wavelengthFalloff: 1
  amplitudeScale: 1
  steepness: 0.3
  seed: 13
  count: Eight
